$$ ExternalConstructorFramework {
    1. Define template struct external_constructor for various value types (boolean, string, binary, numbers, array, object)
    1.1 Each specialization provides a static construct method to initialize a BasicJsonType instance
    1.2 Common steps across specializations:
        - Destroy existing value in j.m_data.m_value
        - Set new value type in j.m_data.m_type
        - Assign new value to j.m_data.m_value
        - Call j.assert_invariant()
}$$

$$ ConstructBoolean -> ExternalConstructorFramework {
    1. Handle boolean value construction
    1.1 Call destroy on existing value
    1.2 Set type to value_t::boolean
    1.3 Assign boolean value
    1.4 Assert invariant
}$$

$$ ConstructString -> ExternalConstructorFramework {
    1. Handle string value construction (const ref, rvalue ref, compatible string types)
    1.1 Call destroy on existing value
    1.2 Set type to value_t::string
    1.3 Assign string value (copy or move)
    1.4 Assert invariant
}$$

