$$ ParseCBORInternal -> ParseInternal {
    1. Handle CBOR major types based on the current byte.
    1.1 For major type 0 (unsigned integer), parse and return the unsigned integer.
    1.2 For major type 1 (negative integer), parse and return the negative integer.
    1.3 For major type 2 (byte string), call get_cbor_binary.
    1.4 For major type 3 (UTF-8 string), call get_cbor_string.
    1.5 For major type 4 (array), call get_cbor_array.
    1.6 For major type 5 (map), call get_cbor_object.
    1.7 For major type 6 (tag), call HandleCBORTags.
    1.8 For major type 7, handle simple values (true, false, null, floats).
}$$

$$ GetCBORString -> GetString {
    1. Determine the length of the CBOR string based on the current byte.
    2. Read the string data based on the determined length.
    3. Handle indefinite-length strings by concatenating chunks.
}$$

$$ GetCBORBinary -> GetBinary {
    1. Determine the length of the CBOR binary data based on the current byte.
    2. Read the binary data based on the determined length.
    3. Handle indefinite-length binary data by concatenating chunks.
}$$

$$ GetCBORArray -> GetArray {
    1. Start a new array with the given length.
    2. If length is indefinite, parse elements until a break byte is encountered.
    3. Parse each element using ParseCBORInternal.
    4. End the array.
}$$

$$ GetCBORObject -> GetObject {
    1. Start a new object with the given length.
    2. If length is indefinite, parse key-value pairs until a break byte is encountered.
    3. Parse each key using GetCBORString and each value using ParseCBORInternal.
    4. End the object.
}$$

