$$ GetUBJSONArray -> GetUBJSONSizeType, GetUBJSONValue { 1. Determine the size and type of the array. 2. Handle BJData ND array encoding as a JData annotated array. 3. Process array elements based on the determined type. 4. Return success or failure based on array creation. }$$

$$ABSTRACT HandleUBJSONErrors { 1. Centralize error handling logic for UBJSON parsing. 2. Provide consistent error messages and parsing error callbacks. }$$

$$ABSTRACT UBJSONParsingLogic { 1. Define the core logic for parsing UBJSON data. 2. Ensure adherence to UBJSON and BJData format specifications. }$$
$$ ProcessUBJSONArray -> ParseUBJSON {
1. Check size_and_type.first != npos
1.1 If true, call sax->start_array(size_and_type.first)
1.2 If false, handle array with unknown size
2. Process array elements based on size_and_type.second
2.1 If size_and_type.second != 0 and != 'N', call get_ubjson_value for each element
2.2 Otherwise, call parse_ubjson_internal for each element
3. Handle array with unknown size
3.1 Call sax->start_array(static_cast<std::size_t>(-1))
3.2 Process elements until current != ']'
3.3 Call parse_ubjson_internal and get_ignore_noop for each element
4. Call sax->end_array()
}$$

$$ ProcessUBJSONObject -> ParseUBJSON {
1. Get size_and_type using get_ubjson_size_type
2. Validate size_and_type for BJData format
3. Process object elements based on size_and_type.first
3.1 If size_and_type.first != npos, call sax->start_object(size_and_type.first)
3.2 Process elements with known size
3.2.1 Call get_ubjson_string and sax->key for each key
3.2.2 Call get_ubjson_value or parse_ubjson_internal based on size_and_type.second
3.3 Process elements with unknown size
3.3.1 Call sax->start_object(static_cast<std::size_t>(-1))
3.3.2 Process elements until current != '}'
3.3.3 Call get_ubjson_string, sax->key, and parse_ubjson_internal for each element
4. Call sax->end_object()
}$$

$$ ParseHighPrecisionNumber -> ParseUBJSON {
1. Get size of number string using get_ubjson_size_value
2. Read number string into number_vector
3. Parse number string using number_lexer
4. Validate parsing result
5. Call appropriate sax->number_* function based on result_number
}$$

