$$ InitializeJSONValue -> { 1. Set m_data.m_type to value_t::null, 2. Set m_data.m_value to default }$$

$$ CreateJSONValue -> parent: InitializeJSONValue { 1. Set m_data.m_type based on input, 2. Set m_data.m_value based on input, 3. Call set_parents, 4. Call assert_invariant }$$

$$ CopyJSONValue -> parent: InitializeJSONValue { 1. Copy m_data.m_type from source, 2. Copy m_data.m_value based on type, 3. Call set_parents, 4. Call assert_invariant }$$

$$ MoveJSONValue -> parent: InitializeJSONValue { 1. Move m_data from source, 2. Invalidate source m_data, 3. Call set_parents, 4. Call assert_invariant }$$

$$ AssignJSONValue -> { 1. Swap m_data.m_type with source, 2. Swap m_data.m_value with source, 3. Call base class assignment, 4. Call set_parents, 5. Call assert_invariant }$$

$$ DestroyJSONValue -> { 1. Call assert_invariant with false }$$

$$ CreateEmptyValue -> parent: CreateJSONValue { 1. Set m_data.m_type to input value_t, 2. Set m_data.m_value to default }$$

$$ CreateNullValue -> parent: CreateJSONValue { 1. Set m_data.m_type to value_t::null, 2. Set m_data.m_value to default }$$

$$ CreateValueFromCompatibleType -> parent: CreateJSONValue { 1. Call JSONSerializer::to_json with input, 2. Call set_parents, 3. Call assert_invariant }$$

