$$ CreateContainerFromInitializerList -> parent: CreateJSONValue { 1. Determine if list represents object or array, 2. Set m_data.m_type accordingly, 3. Populate m_data.m_value based on type, 4. Call set_parents, 5. Call assert_invariant }$$

$$ CreateBinaryArray -> parent: CreateJSONValue { 1. Set m_data.m_type to value_t::binary, 2. Set m_data.m_value to input binary data, 3. Call set_parents, 4. Call assert_invariant }$$

$$ CreateArrayFromInitializerList -> parent: CreateJSONValue { 1. Set m_data.m_type to value_t::array, 2. Populate m_data.m_value.array from input, 3. Call set_parents, 4. Call assert_invariant }$$

$$ CreateObjectFromInitializerList -> parent: CreateJSONValue { 1. Set m_data.m_type to value_t::object, 2. Populate m_data.m_value.object from input, 3. Call set_parents, 4. Call assert_invariant }$$

$$ CreateArrayWithCountCopies -> parent: CreateJSONValue { 1. Set m_data.m_type to value_t::array, 2. Populate m_data.m_value.array with count copies of value, 3. Call set_parents, 4. Call assert_invariant }$$

$$ CreateValueFromIteratorRange -> parent: CreateJSONValue { 1. Validate iterators, 2. Determine type from first iterator, 3. Populate m_data.m_value based on type, 4. Call set_parents, 5. Call assert_invariant }$$

